data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"The SVD writes a matrix as a sum of rank-one terms, sorted from largest to smallest. Keeping the largest terms keeps\nthe most important structure. Because the singular vectors are orthonormal, the discarded terms are orthogonal to the\nkept ones, so the error is the length of what you dropped."},"hints_note":null}

