data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Let $A = U \\Sigma V^\\top$ be the economy SVD, with singular values $s_1 \\ge s_2 \\ge \\dots$. The truncation is\n$A_k = \\sum_{i \\le k} s_i u_i v_i^\\top$. The Frobenius error is $\\lVert A - A_k \\rVert_F = \\sqrt{\\sum_{i > k} s_i^2}$.\nCheck the edge cases: $k = 0$ keeps nothing, and the sums over empty ranges are zero."},"hints_note":null}

